.el .ds Aq '
.TH ifg-release 1  "ifg-release 0.9.0" 
.SH NAME
ifg\-release \- Work with releases and their assets
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBifg release\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Work with releases and their assets
.PP
`release download` verifies every asset against the server\-provided SHA\-256 and deletes it on mismatch. `release create` uploads files with a streaming request, so large artifacts do not sit in memory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
ifg\-release\-list(1)
List releases
.TP
ifg\-release\-view(1)
Show one release (by tag) with its assets
.TP
ifg\-release\-create(1)
Create a release and optionally upload files
.TP
ifg\-release\-upload(1)
Upload files as assets of a release
.TP
ifg\-release\-edit(1)
Edit a release\*(Aqs title, notes or flags
.TP
ifg\-release\-delete(1)
Delete a release (asks for confirmation unless \-\-yes)
.TP
ifg\-release\-download(1)
Download release assets (SHA\-256 verified) into the current directory
.TP
ifg\-release\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.9.0
